2. Normal eGFR, urinary protein \> 3.5 g/day despite ACEI/ARB treatment for 6 months with \ 50 RU/mL; Refractory membranous nephropathy: inadequate response or resistance to prior immunosuppressive therapy (including corticosteroids and/or cytotoxic agents, immunosuppressants and/or biologics), defined as persistent urinary protein ≥ 3.5 g/day with \ 5 years).
