14. Autologous hematopoietic stem cell transplantation (Auto-HSCT) within 12 weeks before initiating GNC-038 treatment;
15. Current use of immunosuppressive therapy;
16. Radiotherapy within 4 weeks before initiating GNC-038 treatment;
17. Chemotherapy or small-molecule targeted therapy within 2 weeks or 5 half-lives prior to treatment;
18. CAR-T therapy within 12 weeks before initiating GNC-038 treatment;
19. Use of any other investigational drug in a clinical trial within 4 weeks or 5 half-lives before the first dose of this study;
20. Any other condition deemed unsuitable for participation in this clinical trial by the investigator.

Inclusion Criteria:

1. PCOS of childbearing age (24-45 years old);
2. non-obesity;
3. After 6 months of metformin (at least 1000-1500 mg/d) intervention, the normal menstrual cycle was still not restored.
4. No drug intervention except metformin was used in last 3 monthes:
5. There is a pregnancy plan within 1 years.
6. The pregnancy test was negative.
7. Heart and liver function is normal, thyroid function is normal, adrenal function is normal.
8. The GnRH stimulation test confirmed that the pituitary and ovarian reserve function was good.
9. Chromosome examination is normal.
10. Did not take part in other clinical trials.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. PCOS was not diagnosed.
2. Severe liver and kidney dysfunction (ALT is 2.5 times greater than normal upper limit, or Cr \> 132 umol/l, or eGFR \ III);
4. Kallmann syndrome, secondary hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, acquired central nervous system diseases, infertility caused by hypothalamic amenorrhea and other secondary infertility;
5. Has a history of abuse of active substances, including alcohol and a history of alcohol related diseases in the past 2 years.
6. Previous history of central nervous system and gonad-related surgery, or other central nervous system and gonad-related surgery (such as central nervous system tumor resection, ovarian chocolate cyst resection) within one year, or other non-central nervous system and gonad surgery within six months;
7. In the past five years, there have been organ system tumors (except for local cutaneous basal cell carcinomas) that have been treated or not treated, regardless of whether there is evidence of local recurrence or metastasis;
8. Hypoglycemic drugs, contraceptives (Dain, Marvelon), ovulation-promoting drugs (clomiphene, letrozole), emergency contraceptives and sex hormone drugs have been or are being used to adjust menstrual cycle and promote ovulation except metformin.
9. Pregnancy;
10. GnRH stimulation test confirmed pituitary and ovarian reserve dysfunction.
11. Abnormal chromosome detection.
12. Patients who are allergic to drugs with similar chemical structure.

Inclusion Criteria:

1. Signed informed consent before the trial, with full understanding of the trial content, procedures, and possible adverse reactions, and self-reported ability to complete the study according to the study requirements;
2. Adult males and females (age ≥18 years, calculated as of the day of signing the informed consent form);
3. Participant body mass index (BMI) = weight (kg)/height² (m²), with BMI within the range of 19.0-26.0 kg/m² (inclusive). Male participants must weigh ≥50 kg, and female participants must weigh ≥45 kg;
4. Agree to use highly effective contraception from the time of signing the informed consent form until 6 months after the last dose of HS-10382, and have no plans for conception or sperm/egg donation during this period.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Have clinically significant abnormalities, as judged by the investigator, in physical examination, vital signs, 12-lead ECG, clinical laboratory tests (complete blood count, blood biochemistry, urinalysis, coagulation function), abdominal ultrasound, etc. during the screening period;
2. Have a history of hepatitis B, hepatitis C, HIV, or syphilis, and/or any one or more clinically significant abnormalities in the four infectious disease screening tests;
3. Have a history of, or current, severe diseases of the nervous system, psychiatric system, digestive system, circulatory system, respiratory system, urinary system, etc., or have new-onset disease before use of the investigational drug, which the investigator considers unsuitable for participation in this study;
4. Have gastrointestinal dysfunction, dysphagia, or a history of surgery affecting drug absorption, distribution, metabolism, or excretion, which the investigator judges unsuitable for enrollment;
5. Have susceptibility to allergic reactions or an allergic constitution (e.g., allergy to pollen, or to two or more drugs/foods), or have a known allergy to the investigational drug or any of its components;
6. Have participated in any other clinical trial and used investigational drugs or devices within 3 months before the first dose;
7. Have donated blood and/or lost more than 200 mL of blood (excluding menstrual blood loss in females) within 3 months before the first dose, and/or received a blood transfusion or blood products, or have plans to donate blood during the study;
8. Have had excessive intake of tea, coffee, and/or caffeine-containing beverages within 3 months before screening (more than 8 cups per day on average, 1 cup = 200 mL), or be unable to stop intake of tea, coffee, and/or caffeine-containing beverages during the study;
9. Have ingested grapefruit or grapefruit products within 48 h before the first dose, or be unable to stop intake of grapefruit or grapefruit products during the study;
10. Have had regular alcohol consumption within 3 months before screening (i.e., more than 14 units of alcohol per week; 1 unit = 14 g alcohol, equivalent to 360 mL beer, 45 mL liquor with 40% alcohol, or 150 mL wine; equivalent to 10 bottles of beer, 1 jin of baijiu, or 3 bottles of red wine per week), or have a positive blood alcohol test, or be unable to stop consumption of alcoholic products during the study;
11. Have smoked more than 5 cigarettes per day on average within 3 months before screening, or be unable to stop use of any tobacco products during the study;
12. Have a history of drug abuse or drug dependence, or have used illicit drugs within 5 years before screening, or have a positive urine drug abuse screening result;
13. Have used any drug that may affect P-gp, BCRP, and/or CYP 2B6 or 3A enzyme activity within 30 days or 5 half-lives of the drug (whichever is longer) before the first dose;
14. Have used any prescription drug, over-the-counter drug, herbal medicine, or health product (except topical preparations with local action) within 14 days before the first dose;
15. Be unable to tolerate venipuncture/indwelling needle blood collection, or have a history of needle or blood phobia;
16. Be breastfeeding within 1 month before screening or during the study, or have a positive pregnancy test result during the screening period (for female participants of childbearing potential);
17. Be likely unable to complete this study for other reasons, or be judged unsuitable for participation by the investigator.

